<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plymouth, Montserrat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Plymouth is the abandoned capital of Montserrat, a British territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. The island's main town and port since colonial times, it was buried under ash and pyroclastic flows by the eruptions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soufriere-hills">Soufrière Hills volcano</a>, which began in 1995 and destroyed the town in 1997. It remains the official capital, though it lies in an exclusion zone and the government works from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brades">Brades</a> in the north.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/plymouth-montserrat.jpg" alt="Plymouth, Montserrat" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xb-70 at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plymouth_Montserrat_Heli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
